{title: Seven Officials}
{subtitle: Esther 1:10–12; 1:13–14; 1:14; 1:16–21}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [C] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The seventh day the [C]wine was [Dm]bright
The king com[C]manded eunuchs to the [Dm]light
To bring the [C]queen with royal [Dm]crown
To show her beauty to the [Bb]town
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But Queen Vashti [C]refused to [Dm]come
Her face a[C]gainst the king's com[Bb]mand
The anger burned [C]within his heart
[Gm]A cri[Am]sis at the court [Dm]apart
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]He sought the wise [C]who knew the times
[Dm]To judge the mat[C]ter in the lines
[Bb]For it was cus[C]tom for the king
[Gm]To ask the laws on which he [Dm]cling
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Carshena Shet[C]har Admat[Bb]ha
Tarshish Meres [C]and Marsena
[Gm]With Memucan [Am]the seven [Bb]men
Holding the high[C]est ranks a[Dm]gain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
Me[Bb]mucan spoke be[C]fore the throne
[Dm]The queen has wronged [C]the king alone
[Bb]But all the officials [C]and the land
Will [Gm]see her refusal in the [Dm]hand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
The [Bb]women will de[C]spise their men
[Dm]And speak the words of [C]her again
[Bb]So let the decree be [C]written out
To [Gm]ban her from the [A]king's ac[Dm]count
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 7}
Give the po[Bb]sition to a [C]woman wise
[Dm]Who is better [C]in his eyes
So [Bb]all the women [C]from the least
Will [Gm]honor every [A]husband's [Dm]beast
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 8}
The [Bb]advice pleased [C]the king and all
[Dm]He did as Memu[C]can did call
And [Bb]wrote the law in [C]Persia's book
To [Gm]seal the fate with iron [Dm]look
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Seven officials [C]held the [Dm]rank
{end_of_verse}

